{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>All this.</b> All that I have said to you — I tested it all with wisdom, and I sought to be yet wiser, and I found that it is a far-off thing. This concerns \"do not be overwise,\" for the essence of what has been is far removed from man's grasp, and what is to come is very deep. Another interpretation: I sought wisdom and found it far off; nevertheless I grasped it and grew wise."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:28:13.558060302Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}